course: dictionary
lesson: 12306
title: A special ceremony
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A coronation is a ceremony, a special event with set steps that people follow. «The coronation took place in Westminster Abbey.» The words Westminster Abbey and the way the sentence sounds show that this is a big, important occasion.
explain: «The crowd cheered when the new queen was crowned at her coronation.» Crowned is the clue. At a coronation, a king or queen is given a crown, so coronation means the whole ceremony where this happens.
explain: Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «The crowd cheered when the new queen was crowned at her ceremony where she is made ruler.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A coronation is the ceremony when a king or queen is crowned and officially becomes ruler.
fact: Coronations are often held in Westminster Abbey, in London.
fact: In history and citizenship lessons, pupils learn about crowns, the anointing and the oath that are part of a coronation.
fact: You might find coronation chicken, a curry-flavoured chicken sandwich filling, at a street party.
fact: «Coronation» is a noun, so you can say «a coronation» or «coronations».
exercise: What does coronation mean? | A kind of curry | A holiday for schools | *The ceremony when a king or queen is crowned | A special party for a birthday
exercise: «The coronation took place in Westminster Abbey.» Where did the coronation take place? | *Westminster Abbey | In a supermarket car park | In a school hall | On a seaside pier
exercise: «The new queen was crowned at her coronation.» What happens at a coronation? | The school closes for a term | A new shop opens | Everyone goes home early | *A king or queen is crowned
test: «We ate coronation chicken sandwiches at the street party.» What is coronation chicken? | A kind of cake with cream | A type of crown | *A curry-flavoured chicken sandwich filling | A song sung in church
test: «Coronation day was a holiday for everyone.» What is coronation day? | The last day of term | A day for sport | *The day a king or queen is crowned | A day for planting trees
exam: Ella says, «The coronation is a crown, right?» What is the best answer? | A coronation is a sandwich filling | Crowns are never worn at a coronation | The crown is the ceremony itself | *The coronation is the whole ceremony, and the crown is one part of it
